{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"final"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MultipleColorSemanticToken"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["        \/\/ Assuming in Figma with have a color semantic token bgPrimary,","        \/\/ two semantic color tokens will be defined in Figma and generated by tokenator.","        \/\/ They can be declared in protocol ColorSemanticTokens,","        \/\/ and defined automaticaly in MISOTheme+ColorSemanticTokens extension","        var bgPrimaryLight: ColorSemanticToken { ColorRawTokens.functionalWhite }","        var bgPrimaryDark: ColorSemanticToken { ColorRawTokens.functionalDarkGray880 }","","        \/\/ Then the develoment team declares an \"higher\" level color semantic token for bgPrimary","        \/\/ inside ColorMultipleSemanticTokens protocol,","        \/\/ and defined inside MISOTheme+ColorMultipleSemanticToken extension","        var bgPrimary: MultipleColorSemanticToken { MultipleColorSemanticToken(light: bgPrimaryLight, dark: bgPrimaryDark) }","","        \/\/ If the same color is used whatever the color scheme is","        var bgPrimary: MultipleColorSemanticToken { MultipleColorSemanticToken(bgPrimaryLight) }","","        \/\/ The theme exposes both generated color semantic tokens and \"crafted\" higher level color semantic tokens.","        \/\/ It is recommended to use the higher level version as it is less error-prone."]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["     @Environment(\\.theme) var theme","     @Environment(\\.colorScheme) var colorScheme","","    \/\/ Given you want to apply the color token \"surfaceBrandPrimary\"","    var body: some View {","        \/\/ Apply the token of color for the view without managing yourself the color scheme","        SomeView()","            .background(theme.colors.surfaceBrandPrimary)","","        \/\/ Or also foregroundStyle(), foregroundColor(), accentColor(), ...","    }"]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["    \/\/ Or get the token depending to the color scheme and do whatever you want with","    theme.colors.surfaceBrandPrimary.color(for: colorScheme)"]},{"style":"note","name":"Since","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS 0.8.0"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/objc(cs)NSObject"],"type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships"},{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/objc(pl)NSObject","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s7CVarArgP","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/SQ","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/SH","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Class","title":"MultipleColorSemanticToken","modules":[{"name":"Tokens for semantics"}],"symbolKind":"class","role":"symbol","platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","beta":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","unavailable":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"macOS","beta":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","unavailable":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"tvOS","beta":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","unavailable":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"visionOS","beta":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"watchOS","beta":false,"introducedAt":"11.0","unavailable":false}],"externalID":"c:@M@MISOTokensSemantic@objc(cs)MultipleColorSemanticToken","fragments":[{"text":"cla